\begin{abstract}
Let $H$ be an $n$-generated numerical semigroup such that its tangent cone $\gr_{\mathfrak m} K[H]$ is defined by quadratic relations.

\begin{eqnarray*}
 \langle 8, 4u', 4u+2u', 4u''+2u+ u', 6u+7u'+4u''-8 \rangle, \text{ or} \\
 \langle 8, 4u', 4u+2u', 4u''+2u+3u', 6u+9u'+4u''-8 \rangle,
\end{eqnarray*}

\label{thm:bounds}
(\cite[1.1, 1.9, 1.12]{HeS-quad})
Let $H$ be a quadratic numerical semigroup minimally generated by $n>1$ elements and $K[H]$ its semigroup ring. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item [(i)] $n \leq e(H) \leq 2^{n-1}$;
\item [(ii)] $e(H)=n$ \ifmmode\Longleftrightarrow \else \unskip${}\Longleftrightarrow{}$\ignorespaces\fi $I_H^*$ has a linear resolution;
\item [(iii)] $e(H)=2^{n-1}$ \ifmmode\Longleftrightarrow \else \unskip${}\Longleftrightarrow{}$\ignorespaces\fi $I_H^*$ is a CI ideal \ifmmode\Longleftrightarrow \else \unskip${}\Longleftrightarrow{}$\ignorespaces\fi $I_H$ is a CI ideal;
\item [(iv)] if $\gr_{\mathfrak m} K[H]$ is Cohen-Macaulay and $e(H) <2^{n-1}$, then $e(H) \leq 2^{n-1}-2^{n-3}$.
\end{enumerate}
Moreover, if we are in any of the situations from $(ii)$, $(iii)$ or  if $\gr_{\mathfrak m} K[H]$ is Cohen-Macaulay and  $e(H) = 2^{n-1}-2^{n-3}$ then $H$ is $G$-quadratic, hence Koszul.

{\em
\label{rem:minimal}
With notation as above, if $e(H)=n$, then   $\gr_{\mathfrak m} K[H]$ has minimal multiplicity and by Sally's \cite[Theorem 2]{Sally-cm} we get that $\gr_{\mathfrak m} K[H]$ is Cohen-Macaulay.
We refer to the proof of Proposition 1.3 in \cite{HeS-quad} for related properties.
}

